
### 4.1 Fast Path (Underlying Ingestion & Quoting)
- Written in lock-free C++ (single-threaded or pinned core using cache-line aligned shared data).
- Receives spot updates, applies current cached Greeks via Taylor expansion, checks inventory skew, and fires outbound quotes.
- Target latency: 1–25 microseconds per tick.

### 4.2 Slow Path (Calibration & Volatility Surface)
- Runs asynchronously on worker threads (e.g., every 500ms–5s, or when significant market events occur).
- Solves implied volatilities via Newton-Raphson / Halley's method for all strikes in the chain.
- Fits the SVI/SABR parameters and updates Greek values in double-buffered or RCU (Read-Copy-Update) structures consumed by the fast loop.

